  Let $\mu_{\parallel \nu} = \left(\frac{\partial \mu}{\partial \nu}\right) \cdot \nu$.
  Then for $(\nu \otimes \eta)$-almost all $z$, $\frac{d (\mu_{\parallel \nu} \otimes \kappa)}{d (\nu \otimes \eta)}(z) = \frac{d (\mu \otimes \kappa)}{d (\nu \otimes \eta)}(z)$.
